{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1251239-jumanji-the-keeper","id":1251239,"title":"Jumanji, the Keeper","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-03T17:20:10-07:00","id":1251239,"title":"Jumanji, the Keeper","content":"Jumanji is one of the most powerful Keepers of Arcadia. It has a need to kidnap people through games and make them suffer their ordeals in a gameplay fashion with a jungle setting, because it apparently feeds itself from the thrill of &quot;ADVENTURE&quot;! Therefoe, whatever form or title Jumanji has, it will always have gameplay features and it will be themed in a stereotypical western vision of African jungles. It has five titles which are explained below [SPOILERS from the movies]:<br /> <br /> 1. The Realm: the Jumanji realm is a wild jungle filled with natural perils. It is angry and savage nature, both beautiful and dangerous. This Realm can be destroyed by taking the &quot;Jaguar's Eye&quot;, a powerful jewel, from its shrine, a giant jaguar statue. The Realm has a goblin market filled that looks like an exotic bazaar.<br /> 2. The Savage Wisps: Jumanji is also all the wild and savage beasts that live in the jungle. White rhinos, angry hippos, elephants, lions, carnivorous plants, playful monkeys, jaguars, snakes, pythons, crocodiles... Most are very hostile and extremely deadly.<br /> 3. The Human Wisps: These are Jumanji's NPCs used to guide the changelings towards gameplay objectives. They give messages, sell items, offer transport and give other important services to keep the narrative flowing. They have very limited interaction and are obviously seen as NPCs (or eidolons) when they repeat their sentences over and over.<br /> 4. Prop: Jumanji has a phisical object that sometimes looks like a boardgame. It is located not in Arcadia but in the mortal world. This old looking boardgame twists the fate of anyone playing it, making some or all players fall into Jumanji's Realm if they get a lucky number on the dice. This object can sometimes change its Mask in order to make itself more attractive to the type of game a victim is more willing to play.<br /> 5. Actor: nobody has ever seen a personal representation of Jumanji, so this is mostly a legend. Some people say Jumanji can take the form of a giant elephant, or rhino, twice the size of its normal counterpart. Others say it can take the form of a normal looking person who lives in the mortal world and carries the boardgame around and leave it in unsuspicious locations.<br /> <br /> Jumanji has a very defined Modus Operandi: it kidnaps people by looking like a harmless game (whatever type of game the victims like) and then make them suffer an ordeal until the game is finished. The game has a particular preference for children and teenagers that misbehave or act in a problematic way, so any child or teenager getting willpoint for satisfying their Vice near the game will probably be attracted to it (by hearing ominous drumbeats coming from the object).<br /> The game may decide to make any player or all the players fall directly into the Jumanji Realm. This Realm, situated in Arcadia, has its own sense of time. People can be there for few months, while many years are passing in the outside world.<br /> Jumanji is a bit different, scarier and even more powerful than &quot;common&quot; Gentry because it isn't afraid of showing its power and terror in the mortal world. It can unleash its minions on mortal streets without care for the consequences.<br /> However completing the Jumanji game has a powerful time effect on all the players and the mortal world around them. Everyone is taken back to the time where they started playing the game and the world gets back to normal with mortals forgetting the chaos unleashed on the streets.<br /> Mortals that endured the game inside the Jungle are turned into changelings. Most become Beasts. A particular effect of Jumaanji is that the Mask can become totally different from the original human body, so that a small framed kid can have a Mask that look like the Rock while a teenage girl can have the mask of a male middle-aged person. Escaping the Jumanji Realm will not turn the changelings back to human, they have to finish the game, and it is unclear if finishing the game will turn the players back to human form.<br /> Jumanji also assigns its very special huntsman to hunt the players, Van Pelt, who keeps changing appearances: sometimes he looks like a stereotypical english hunter, or like a brooding mercenary, but he always has a firearm and jungle gear as his panoply.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24237-pluvinarch","name":"Pluvinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T17:50:38-07:00","id":1251245,"title":"","content":"I think most of the other Titles are perhaps a little over-Remember that not every bit of land need be a Realm but can instead be a Domain, which still has prominent power, and likewise that not every creature must be expressed as a Wisp or Actor as well, not when there are the Domain equivalents of Eidolons, changelings (including loyalists!), Hobgoblins(including Hedge Beasts!), and Hedge Ghosts to employ-but yeah, the prop of Jumanji of is a <i>dangerously </i>powerful one, since it basically instantly shortcuts from Ironside to it's Domain on top of it's hyper-potent Contracts.<br /> <br /> Also, good call on Van Pelt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}